  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thandanani Community based OVC Care &amp; Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project goal: Communities in Msunduzi (Pietermaritzburg) and Richmond in the Midlands of KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa respond to the basic material, physical, cognitive and emotional needs of orphans and vulnerable children (OVC).
Outcomes: 
1. Community based volunteers are capacitated and supported to provide effective care and support services to OVC households within their community
2. Increased access to professional welfare services and therapeutic programs by at least 2000 OVC through the support of caregivers.
3. At least 6 capacitated community based Early Learning Centres provide effective care and support to pre-school aged children within their communities.

The Community Based Orphans and Vulnerable Children Care and Support Programme is being executed by Thandanani Children Foundation is KwaZulu Natal Province. The second phase of this project seeks to support more than 5000 OVC and 1000 caregivers through capacity building, direct support, social services delivery and early childhood development. Through this work, Thandanani, together with other like minded organisations intend to use gained knowledge, experience and evidence gathered to advocate and campaign for the rights of OVC within the province. This project will be linked to provincial and national initiatives aimed at transforming the lives of OVC and approaches currently being used by duty bearers. Further, the project will foster a greater responsibility towards the communities as their knowledge base will be increased through innovative practices such as accompaniment and immersion.</narrative>
  </description>
